  "source_and_output_review": [
    {
      "rule": "Diagnostic redaction must not mutate private protocol or publication ownership, and preserving exact private values must not expose them through public result projections.",
      "files": [
        "lib/execution_io.mjs",
        "lib/execution.mjs",
        "lib/execution_result.mjs",
        "lib/execution_journal.mjs",
        "lib/commands/serve.mjs",
        "lib/task_prepare.mjs",
        "test/execution-backends.test.mjs",
        "docs/execution.md"
      ],
      "boundaries_checked": [
        "Collection validates the exact remote job/root/input head/session and terminal outcome before redaction; canonical task/run identities override returned metadata. Cached collection revalidates these fields before adoption.",
        "Private result taskId, runId, providerJobId, sessionId, turnId, inputHead, repo, branch and pushedHead are preserved verbatim. Publication still validates original repository, owned branch, revision and artifact hashes before mutation; redaction cannot turn unowned input into an owned surrogate.",
        "Outcome, lines, usage, PR diagnostic text and the generated artifact summary remain redacted. Raw artifacts retain exact bytes and hashes in mode 0600 results. Inputs and supplied secret lists are unchanged.",
        "Local collect uses the same helper; local settlement already writes exact validated identities with redacted diagnostics. Five CLI adapters, preassigned and discovered session readers, saved result replay and continuation retain native identities.",
        "Remote applyCollectedResult adopts exact owned session IDs; both reserved provider fixtures publish against the pre-collection snapshot and continue the same session after restart with one collection and one initial fixture submission.",
        "The result route builds its existing bounded summary, then sanitizes the entire response using the execution/run supplied secrets with recognized-credential fallback for standalone readers. Ownership, application checkpoints and verification output are public-redacted without rewriting private files or calling a provider.",
        "Journal projections and verification diagnostics still apply normal redaction. Preparation reads exact owned sessions but separately sanitizes outcome and usage. Artifact retention and cancellation do not determine routing identity.",
        "Private result/execution ownership remains exact for credential-shaped and secret-equal fixture IDs, while public result, journal output and verification diagnostic projections redact them. Foreign sessions, contradictory terminal outcomes, absent results, invalid manifests and stopped tasks retain the existing rejection/quarantine paths.",
        "Previously rewritten cached identities require restoring exact ownership from recorded acknowledgement/provider evidence without erasing intents or redispatching. No automatic reconstruction, transport availability, live model/plugin qualification, permissions or merge authority is claimed."
      ],
      "regressions": [
        "result metadata redaction preserves exact private ownership while cleaning diagnostics",
        "opaque remote identities survive collection, publication and continuation while public results stay redacted",
        "opaque local identities survive settlement, collection and cached continuation without diagnostic exposure",
        "foreign sessions cannot enter observation, collection, cache or continuation ownership",
        "private artifact payloads and paths stay out of result projections and verification diagnostics"
      ]
    }
  ],
